			<h2
				id="failures"
				class="mb-4 font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl"
			>
				When it does not come up
			</h2>
			<p class="mb-8 max-w-3xl font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
				Every install failure on this page announces itself in one of six ways. The proxy's
				own stderr goes to
				<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">~/.hermes/aphrodite/proxy-stderr.log</code>
				- read that file before anything else.
			</p>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto">
				<table class="w-full border-collapse font-mono text-base">
					<thead>
						<tr class="border-b-2 border-oxblood-dark text-left">
							<th class="py-3 pr-4 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-stamped-canary">SYMPTOM</th>
							<th class="py-3 pr-4 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-stamped-canary">CAUSE</th>
							<th class="py-3 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-stamped-canary">FIX</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="text-bone-newsprint">
						<tr class="border-b border-oxblood-dark">
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-bone-white">the plugin logs the setup command and stays disabled</td>
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-zinc-dust">binaries missing from ~/.hermes/aphrodite/binaries/</td>
							<td class="py-3">bash download.sh (or pwsh ./download.ps1) in the plugin folder</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-oxblood-dark">
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-bone-white">download.sh stops at the verify step</td>
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-zinc-dust">checksum does not match SHA256SUMS.txt</td>
							<td class="py-3">re-run the script; check network access to GitHub Releases</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-oxblood-dark">
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-bone-white">no API key configured</td>
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-zinc-dust">no aphrodite.toml in the working directory</td>
							<td class="py-3">--api-key or APHRODITE_API_KEY</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-oxblood-dark">
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-bone-white">port already in use</td>
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-zinc-dust">another proxy already bound to 9797/9798</td>
							<td class="py-3">tail proxy-stderr.log; APHRODITE_CACHE_PORT / APHRODITE_TOKEN_PORT</td>
						</tr>
						<tr class="border-b border-oxblood-dark">
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-bone-white">the binary is SIGKILLed on launch (macOS)</td>
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-zinc-dust">quarantine, or no Xcode Command Line Tools</td>
							<td class="py-3">re-run aphrodite setup - ditto, xattr -c, ad-hoc codesign</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-bone-white">a health-poll warning after launch</td>
							<td class="py-3 pr-4 text-zinc-dust">a port did not answer within 5 seconds</td>
							<td class="py-3">the warning names the port; check proxy-stderr.log</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-dust">
				Before launching, the plugin probes both ports' /health endpoints and skips the launch
				when another process already answers a confirmed Aphrodite health body - so a second
				Hermes session does not start a second proxy pair. A failed registration is a warning,
				never an abort.
			</p>
